sequenceDiagram
  %% Target design: ADR 0243/0244 task, one Swamp run, agent-observer-swamp-acts, root-of-trust-gateway-only, Ansible phases for idempotent Node state (rule 22). docs/reference/node-provisioning.md#add-a-node.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: node:add
  %% kind: node.add
  %% Verification: https://github.com/hardimpactdev/orbit/blob/main/swamp/proof/node/add.cases.yaml
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  %% lane HUB icon=server pill=target tone=purple
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as Node<br/>reached over ssh
  participant HUB as WireGuard hub<br/>vpn Node
  CLI->>GW: node:add NAME
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit node:add NAME`
  %%> - syntax: `<name> [host] [--host-key-fingerprint=SHA256] [--ssh-port=PORT] [--user=USER] [--orbit-user=USER] [--platform=PLATFORM] [--architecture=ARCH] [--tld=TLD] [--role=ROLE]... [--cluster=ID] [--wireguard-ip=IP] [--lan-ip=IP] [--wireguard-endpoint=HOST:PORT] [--dns-server=IP] [--setting=PATH:VALUE] [--json]`
  Note over GW: Validate, reserve the name
  %%> Requirements:
  %%> - a missing name record means new enrollment, not an unknown-Node refusal
  %%> - authority follows /cli/node#authority; existing-target access needs Gateway authority or a grant to that Node
  %%> - admission reads recorded state, with the existing lifecycle lock, worker renewal and firewall ownership rules
  alt caller has no authority
    %% path: caller-refused
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>node_access.required
  else unsupported platform or requested architecture
    %% path: platform-refused
    GW--xCLI: Platform refused
    %%> Codes:
    %%> - node.platform_unsupported or node.architecture_unsupported
  else account or existing Mac address invalid
    %% path: account-refused
    GW--xCLI: Account refused
    %%> Codes:
    %%> - node.invalid_linux_user, node.user_change_unsupported, node.macos_account_required, node.macos_account_mismatch or node.wireguard_required
  else TLD, role, Cluster or network intent invalid
    %% path: configuration-refused
    GW--xCLI: Configuration refused
    %%> Codes:
    %%> - node.tld_required, node.tld_invalid, node.tld_taken, node.tld_conflict, node.role_conflict, cluster.not_found, cluster.membership_conflict or cluster.lan_ip_conflict
  else approved identity missing or different
    %% path: identity-refused
    GW--xCLI: Identity refused
    %%> Codes:
    %%> - node.ssh_host_fingerprint_required or node.ssh_host_key_mismatch; no new approval replaces a recorded pin
  else existing Node owns Instances
    %% path: has-instances
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>node.has_instances
  else lifecycle already in progress
    %% path: lifecycle-busy
    GW--xCLI: Refused<br/>node.provisioning_busy
  else admitted
    %% path: admitted
    Note over GW: Record enrollment intent
    %%> Result:
    %%> - each refusal above creates no Operation or run and changes no records or machine state
    %%> - a new Node is provisioning; an existing Node keeps its prior identity until the full check succeeds
    %%> - freeze the role set (recorded plus requested), settings, network and publication resources; no child Operations
    GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-node-add
    %%> Secrets:
    %%> - only vault key names enter the run; bootstrap identity and observer secret stay at the existing vault boundary
    %%> - certificate signing stays at the Gateway; no root-of-trust key leaves it
    GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>Operation ID
    SW->>N: Read the host key<br/>SSH · first contact
    %%> Why first:
    %%> - first contact ignores worker known_hosts; no machine mutation precedes approval
    SW->>SW: Require approved host key<br/>native assert
    %%> Result:
    %%> - all later connections pin the approved key; a mismatch stops before changing either SSH pin or the machine
    alt Linux enrollment
      %% path: linux
      SW->>SW: Write the playbook input<br/>phase: input
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - creates private inventory, vars, known_hosts and vault-derived files in this run's folder
      SW->>N: Set up the machine<br/>Ansible phase: baseline
      %%> Before mutation:
      %%> - read platform, architecture and bootstrap account; require Linux x86_64 and any supplied architecture to match
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - manage the account, validated sudo rule, control keys, base packages and kernel policy
      %%> - preserve public recovery SSH while applying the managed firewall
      SW->>N: Set up the tunnel<br/>Ansible phase: tunnel
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - keep the Node's private key on the Node; return its unique public key with the phase result
      %%> - an existing hub keeps its peer-facing key; matching tunnel resources are reused
      opt Linux peer joins the VPN hub
        %% path: hub-peer
        SW->>HUB: Add the peer<br/>Ansible phase: hub
        %%> What it does:
        %%> - write only the joining peer's file in orbit-peers.d and apply that peer without restarting the hub
        %%> - preserve the hub key, loader and unrelated peers, including file-only peers
        %%> On failure:
        %%> - a written peer remains; a new attempt reuses it
      end
      SW->>N: Install the Node agent<br/>Ansible phase: agent
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - install the pinned observer binary, configuration and secret; start after the tunnel unit
      SW->>N: Verify managed access<br/>Ansible phase: managed
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - reach the same machine as the managed user over WireGuard with passwordless sudo
      opt eligible CLI plan
        %% path: cli-publication
        SW->>N: Publish the Orbit CLI<br/>Ansible phase: cli
        %%> Best effort:
        %%> - allow failure of this phase; role work, DNS and the final check still run
      end
      opt frozen role set is nonempty
        %% path: requested-roles
        SW->>N: Converge each role<br/>Ansible phase: roles
        %%> What it does:
        %%> - apply frozen role work even without --role; use the existing role and firewall ownership rules
        %%> - the first role closes public recovery SSH only after managed access works
      end
      opt DNS needs publication
        %% path: dns-publication
        SW->>HUB: Configure DNS backend<br/>Ansible phase: dns
        SW->>HUB: Install DNS listener<br/>Ansible phase: dns-listener
        SW->>N: Publish private DNS<br/>Ansible phase: dns-publish
        %%> Order:
        %%> - publish only after frozen roles are ready; a new hub's DNS listener precedes private names
      end
      SW->>N: Check the Node state<br/>Ansible phase: check
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - collect the agent, binary, observer-secret and tunnel evidence; wait up to 20 s for a peer handshake
      %%> - the hub needs no handshake with itself; this is the only final machine-state check
    else --platform=macos
      %% path: macos
      SW->>N: Read the platform<br/>SSH argv
      SW->>SW: Bind the Node identity<br/>native validation
      %%> Requirements:
      %%> - Darwin x86_64 or arm64; any requested architecture matches the observation
      SW->>N: Verify Mac managed access<br/>SSH argv
      SW->>N: Inspect the Mac tunnel<br/>SSH argv
      %%> What it does:
      %%> - verify the same existing account and the existing WireGuard address; retain the documented native macOS path
      %%> - no Ansible, sudo, agent, role, account, tunnel, DNS or firewall mutation
    end
    SW->>SW: Check the Node<br/>native assert
    %%> What it does:
    %%> - assert the phase evidence for the admitted platform; the Gateway projects this one terminal result
    opt Linux input may exist, on success or failure
      %% path: cleanup
      SW->>SW: Remove the playbook input<br/>phase: cleanup
      %%> Order:
      %%> - wait for all dependent phases and their cleanup to settle before removing this run's private folder
      %%> - preserve the original failure and report incomplete cleanup; macOS has no input folder
    end
    alt full check succeeds
      %% path: succeeded
      SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
      Note over GW: Record the Node active
      %%> Result:
      %%> - project observed architecture, approved SSH pins and WireGuard public key, frozen role results and settings
      %%> - repeat enrollment re-converges and checks the same eligible Node without duplicate identities or resources; it is not an admission skip
    else approval or platform check fails
      %% path: pre-mutation-failed
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>identity or platform error
      %%> Result:
      %%> - no machine mutation; a new Node remains failed, and an existing Node keeps its prior identity and status
    else a later phase or final check fails
      %% path: phase-failed
      SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error_code · failed step
      Note over GW: Retain the failed result
      %%> Result:
      %%> - a new Node stays failed; an existing Node keeps its prior identity and status
      %%> - unfinished assignments created by this request stay failed, with the native failed-step label
      %%> Recovery:
      %%> - completed and partial work remains, with no rollback; after fixing the cause, start a new attempt of the same command
    end
  end
